{# Content slot: the canonical out-of-network line, the two rate cards (associates and
   Kay, separately), the Superbill explanation, sliding-scale and cancellation notes,
   the plain-text /faq pointer, and the hand-written Service + PriceSpecification. #}
{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <p>{{ site.positioning.outOfNetworkLine }}</p>
  <p>Two specifics worth having up front. We do not accept HMO or EPO plans. If you have a PPO with out-of-network mental health benefits, we can provide a Superbill for each session that you submit yourself. And the part people are most often surprised by: your insurance company, not our office, decides whether you are reimbursed and how much.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <h2>Which rate applies to you</h2>
  <p>Two things decide it: who you see, and how long the session runs. Sessions with Kay are priced differently from sessions with the associate therapists she trains and supervises, and 50, 75 and 90 minute sessions are priced separately again. Not sure which row is yours? That is one of the things the free call is for. We will talk through what is going on, who is the right fit, and what length actually suits the work, and you will know the number before you book anything.</p>
{% endcall %}

