{% call s.prose({ width: "narrow" }) %}
  <h2>About Superbills and reimbursement</h2>
  <p>We do not require a diagnosis in order to begin therapy with us. If you choose to submit claims to your insurance company, your insurer may require diagnostic information for reimbursement. That is their requirement rather than ours, and it is worth knowing before you decide how you want to pay.</p>
  <p>We can provide a Superbill for each session: an itemized receipt you can submit to your PPO insurance for out-of-network reimbursement. To be clear, we don't bill your insurance for you, and we can't promise what they'll reimburse, since that depends on your specific plan. Many PPO plans reimburse a meaningful portion of out-of-network care. It's worth a quick call to your insurer to ask about your out-of-network mental health benefits.</p>
  <h2>Sliding scale, payment, and cancellations</h2>
  <p>A sliding scale is available on a limited basis, handled quietly between you and your therapist. We accept cash, check, Venmo, Zelle, and all major credit cards. We ask for 24 hours' notice to change or cancel a session, since a reserved hour that goes unused can't be given to someone else on short notice; without that notice, the full session fee applies.</p>
  <p>Still have questions about what to expect? Our <a href="/faq">full FAQ page</a> covers the ones people ask most, and the free call is the best place to ask anything it does not.</p>
{% endcall %}

